4. Image pipeline VAE — Apache-2.0 (corrected 2026-11-22)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The pipeline's VAE is Apache-2.0. An earlier revision of this file said it was
non-commercial; that was wrong, and the correction is recorded here because the
mistake is easy to repeat.

flux2-vae_small.safetensors (249,521,340 B, 251 tensors)
  License: Apache License 2.0
  Upstream: black-forest-labs/FLUX.2-small-decoder
            file diffusion_pytorch_model.safetensors
  Evidence: HF tree API reports size 249,521,340 and lfs.oid
              d8d52ba036475f5fb07c8b435e176d3d97ebfa82f0d1a1c317f9cc1e25bd013b
            which equals the local sha256 byte for byte, so the local file IS the
            Apache-2.0 release. That repository's cardData.license is apache-2.0
            and its README states both "Available under the Apache 2.0 license."
            and, under a License heading, "This model is licensed under the
            https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0."
  Architecture match: the local MOSS VAE config declares
            "_class_name": "AutoencoderKLFlux2", which is exactly the class the
            upstream README loads with
            AutoencoderKLFlux2.from_pretrained("black-forest-labs/FLUX.2-small-decoder").

  Why the earlier reading was wrong: Comfy-Org/Flux-2-Dev carries a
  repository-level tag of flux-1-dev-non-commercial-license. That tag covers the
  repackaged DiT and the FULL-size decoder in that repo, not this file. The same
  bytes are published by Black Forest Labs separately under Apache-2.0, and
  file-level provenance outranks a repackager's repo-level tag.

flux2-vae.safetensors (full size, 336,213,556 B, sha256 d64f3a68...)
  License: FLUX.1 [dev] Non-Commercial License v1.1.2
  Status: PARKED, NOT SHIPPED. Moved to
          ComfyUI/models/vae/_noncommercial_do_not_ship/ so ComfyUI cannot load it.
  Why: No Apache-2.0 release of the FULL decoder exists. FLUX.2-klein publishes
          only a DiT single-file with no separate VAE, so FLUX.2-small-decoder is
          the only Apache-2.0 decoder BFL ships. The full decoder is available
          only from FLUX.2-dev and the Comfy-Org repack, both non-commercial.
  Full text: licenses/LICENSE-FLUX-NONCOMMERCIAL.md

